<title>USA: Union Pacific, Mobil in alliance.</title>
<headline>Union Pacific, Mobil in alliance.</headline>
<dateline>FORT WORTH, Texas 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Union Pacific Resources Group Inc said Wednesday it has formed an alliance with Mobil Exploration &amp; Producing U.S. Inc to evaluate the oil and natural gas potential of several large tracts in Cameron and Vermillion Parishes, Louisiana.</p>
<p>The companies will each own 50 percent of the partnership. Union Pacific said it will be the designated operator.</p>
<p>Both companies collectively control, either by lease or by option, more than 200,000 acres in the two-parish area.</p>
<p>Mobil Exploration &amp; Producing is a subsidiary of Mobil Corp headquartered in Dallas, Texas.</p>
